00:16:32.000 --> 00:17:17.000
that we hold. We have very strong feelings about how men and women are, and that leads to the idea that women are less competent than men in a lot of these fields that we're talking about. And we have real strong ideas about how they should be, and that leads to this dislike when they go over the line, when they tread where they're not supposed to be. There are other aspects to the double-bind. Female leaders can get in trouble for displaying emotion, but also for not displaying emotion. Lisa Feldman-Barritt is a psychology professor at Northeastern University and author of the book, How Emotions Are Made.
刻板印象的起源。我们对男性的表现和女性的表现有非常强烈的感觉，这导致了这样一种观点：在我们正在讨论的很多领域中，女性不如男性有能力。我们对她们应该是什么样有着非常强烈的看法，当她们越界、涉足不该涉足的领域时，就会导致这种反感。双重约束还有其他方面。女性领导者可能会因为表现出情绪而陷入麻烦，也会因为不表现出情绪而陷入麻烦。莉萨·费尔德曼-巴雷特是东北大学的心理学教授，也是《情绪是如何产生的》一书的作者。

