them as competent but cold. There is something disturbing about these ideas. They ask women who are the victims here to compensate for the biases of others. Many experts also think that a society changes our stereotypes will change as well. If more women make it through the labyrinth and get to the top, fewer people will have trouble seeing women as leaders. Many countries and organizations are coming to think of leadership as being collaborative rather than dictatorial. The less we think of leaders as alpha males, the easier it's going to be for our unconscious minds to see women as leaders. If there's one common thread here, it's that ending the double bind can't be just on the women reaching for high office or the corner office. It has to be on all of us.
她们有能力但冷酷。这些想法有些令人不安。它们要求作为受害者的女性去补偿他人的偏见。许多专家还认为，随着社会的发展，我们的刻板印象也会改变。如果有更多的女性穿过迷宫登上顶峰，就会有更少的人难以将女性视为领导者。许多国家和组织开始将领导力视为协作式而非独裁式的。我们越少把领导者视为阿尔法男性，我们的潜意识就越容易将女性视为领导者。如果这里有一个共同的线索，那就是结束双重约束不能仅仅依靠追求高级公职或核心办公室的女性。这必须靠我们所有人。

